LanguageData.SRABarrierTooltip:
The barrier can block incoming damage.

-Barriers have barrier efficiency. Incoming damage is multiplied by this value before it is used to calculate barrier loss.
-The barrier also takes the unit's incoming damage multiplier into account and multiplies it with barrier efficiency. If the incoming damage multiplier is above 100%, it will not be applied.
-Some barriers have a recharge cooldown. If the barrier is completely destroyed, it enters recharge cooldown. If this cooldown is greater than 0, the barrier will be fully restored immediately when the cooldown ends.
-Some barriers have a damage cap, preventing any single hit from exceeding that value. This only takes effect when the value is greater than 0.
-Some barriers have damage reduction, reducing incoming damage by the specified amount. This only takes effect when the value is greater than 0.

